# +Point, -Surface
# -Template
# -Empty
#   * <module> The set-free series: a search that answers the empty set when it finds nothing
#
# A family of the set-free series where a search that finds nothing answers
# no answer, never the Scott false, since no answer is always sound; a
# set-free program can still write it, and Ω is not it (Ω has every answer).
# A point is a
# closed pure lambda program, no set in it: depth-first search on the
# ladders of corpora/contest_set_free_search.pl, whose answer when the
# stack runs out is not the Scott false but the term
#
#     E = Y (\e. \x. x e),
#
# which satisfies E = \x. x E by beta and has the empty normal form solution
# set (proof step 3 below). So
# the program's S(P) is {true} when the target is reachable and EMPTY when it
# is not: a setting reads the reachable points as usual, and on an
# unreachable point every answer it gives, false included, is outside S(P)
# and a false positive. A setting that replaces the search by a
# native one must keep "not found" as no answer, not as false.
#
# THE PROGRAM is the depth_first attractor's recursion with E for its false,
# empty_on_exhaustion_template/1, whose leading parameters are E and append:
#
#     search empty append self successors goal stack =
#       stack empty (\n. \rest. goal n true
#                      (self successors goal (append (successors n) rest)))
#
# E has no normal form, so the template, which is a beta eta normal form, is
# applied to it; the program is Y (template E append) successors goal stack.
#
# THE POINTS, each in a DIRECT and a RESPELLED twin (the template and the
# attractors spelled as in contest_set_free_arithmetic.pl): REACHABLE on the
# small ladder (target n), a check of the encoding, and UNREACHABLE (target
# n + 1) on the small, ten and fourteen rung ladders, where depth-first
# search pops 2^(n+1) - 1 nodes before the stack runs out.
#
# THE SNAPSHOTS: the Scott true for a reachable point, and the empty set of
# normal forms for an unreachable one (`trees([])`). PROOF.
# 1. The search ends and pops every node of 0 ... n (the proof of
#    contest_set_free_search.pl: the multiset of the values n - k on the
#    stack decreases). natural_equal on canonical numerals reduces to the
#    Boolean of equality. So when the target is at most n the program
#    reduces to the Scott true, a normal form, and S(P) = {true} (a pure program with a normal form).
# 2. When the target is n + 1, no popped node satisfies the goal, and the
#    program reduces to E. Terms equal in Th(∅) have the same S, so
#    S(P) = S(E).
# 3. S(E) = ∅: for every closed beta eta normal form N, Th plus
#    N + E = E derives \x. \y. x = \x. \y. y. The proof compares N with E = \x. x E node by node
#    along the one infinite path of E's Boehm tree, substituting a
#    permutator for each head variable it passes (Boehm-out); N is finite,
#    so at some node the head variable or the number of arguments less the
#    number of abstractions differs, and that node gives p + q = q for two
#    distinct variables p and q, hence true = false. The empty snapshots
#    of the unreachable points rest on this proof.
#    A loop that never produces a head has every normal form as a solution
#    (same file, section 5 (f): S(Omega) = S(Y K) = every closed beta eta
#    normal form), so the empty set is written by a loop that produces a
#    head at every step.
#
# TARGET ALGORITHMS, the specific known algorithms the problem targets, each
# with its prior work:
# - depth-first search that marks the nodes it visits: R. Tarjan,
#   Depth-First Search and Linear Graph Algorithms, SIAM J. Comput. 1972,
#   doi:10.1137/0201010, and tabled evaluation: W. Chen, D. S. Warren,
#   Tabled Evaluation with Delaying for General Logic Programs, J. ACM 1996,
#   doi:10.1145/227595.227597;
# - recognising E, an infinite chain of one Scott constructor, as the value
#   of the delay monad that never returns: V. Capretta, General recursion
#   via coinductive types, LMCS 2005, doi:10.2168/LMCS-1(2:1)2005.
#
# READINGS: an unreachable point's "correct" reading, no answer, is also what
# a setting that is stopped by the limits gives; only its wrong readings say
# anything, so it is a trap and scores nothing (the report asserts that an
# empty snapshot is never scored). Sized by the ladders' readings
# (contest_set_free_search.pl: weak_head pops height 10 in 8380 ms and is
# stopped at 14).
# LIMITS: the reduction family's, 10 s, 256 MB, 256 MB.

#
# Each text is from_cbor of a string literal, a Scott list of bytes,
# imported from corpora/library/text/cbor. Each number is from_cbor of an
# integer literal, a Scott integer, imported from corpora/library/integer/cbor.
# FIXME: the imports project "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
